{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2011_sprinkle_parsley_zhao.y.l_peng.j:0/children/0/children/0/children/0:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2011_sprinkle_parsley_zhao.y.l_peng.j", "subject": "lyracystidae", "text": "Gogiid eocrinoids with ridged thecal plates having few epispires,\nthree lyre- or heart-shaped, erect, exothecal ambulacra with\nendotomous brachioles, and a long, thin, multiplated, attachment\nstalk.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
