{"audit": {"coverageKind": "skeleton", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2011_sprinkle_parsley_zhao.y.l_peng.j:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1:placement", "kind": "placement", "parent": "lyracystidae", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1", "position": 1, "printedAttribution": "as-record", "rank": "genus", "source": "2011_sprinkle_parsley_zhao.y.l_peng.j", "subject": "lyracystis", "tree": "taxonomy"}
{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2011_sprinkle_parsley_zhao.y.l_peng.j:0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "path": "0/children/0/children/0/children/0/children/1", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2011_sprinkle_parsley_zhao.y.l_peng.j", "subject": "lyracystis", "text": "Theca large, cup-shaped to globular, both vertical and horizontal\nprimary ridges present; about 60, small-to-medium, ridged plates\nper side, scattered epispires between ridges; summit domed to\nprotuberant, bearing tiny plates with epispires. Three large,\nlyre-shaped, exothecal ambulacra branching off summit, lateral\ntrunks biserial or triserial, no spines present over wide,\nadoral, food groove; up to 44 brachioles with low cover plates\nattached between trunks. Stalk very long, thin, with small domed,\nridged, or spiny plates, no distal holdfast preserved.\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
